⏺ Committed. Quick summary:

  What changed (iOS only — web and Android untouched):
  - client/src/lib/platform.ts — new isIos() helper (the single gate)
  - client/src/hooks/useAIGeneration.ts — cloud fallback skipped on iOS; FM
  failure shows error + placeholder neighbors
  - client/src/lib/synthesizeMerge.ts — iOS short-circuits to literal-concat
  after FM, never hits cloud
  - client/src/pages/HexmindApp.tsx — local generateNeighbors + refreshNode
  cloud paths gated; loading state cleaned up on FM failure
  - client/src/components/SettingsModal.tsx — provider picker / API-key fields /
   security note hidden on iOS, replaced by single Apple Intelligence status
  card
  - client/src/hooks/useProviderSettings.ts — provider locked to "apple" on iOS,
   /api/providers fetch and setProvider both no-op there

  Verification: 68 tests pass, pnpm check clean, pnpm build clean, npx cap sync 
  ios clean.

  Two commits:
  - 4c87352 — .gitignore for the 361M backup dir
  - cfabcfe — the iOS strip itself

  What I deliberately did NOT touch (per your instructions):
  - The server-side multi-provider proxy (server/llmProxy.ts) — web still uses
  it
  - The provider hook's PROVIDERS list, ApiKeys interface, header builder — web
  still uses them
  - Anything in android/

  Next step in Xcode: rebuild and run on simulator/device. On iOS the Settings →
   AI Provider tab now just shows the Apple Intelligence availability status;
  tile-tap and tile-refresh use FM only and surface a clear toast if FM isn't
  available.

