⏺ Strip is working — every generation in that trace went through
  FoundationModels.generate and not one /api/generate cloud call appeared. Three
   observations from the trace, ordered by what matters:

  1. FM timeout race is too tight (the only functional regression)

  The line that matters:
  ⚡️  [warn] - [FM] on-device failed, caller will fall back: FM timeout after
  12000ms
  ERROR MESSAGE:  {"errorMessage":"FoundationModels generation timed out after
  15s"}

  Our JS-side Promise.race cuts at 12s — but the Swift side has its own 15s
  budget. JS wins the race and aborts before the native call has a chance to
  either succeed or surface its real error. Pre-strip this was harmless because
  the cloud fallback caught it; post-strip the user just sees "On-device
  returned unparseable output" and gets nothing. Fix: bump JS timeout above
  native so native errors actually propagate.

  2. ANE transient failure underneath

  ANE inference operation failed with status=0x15 : Program Inference error

  This is a Neural Engine hardware-level failure on a single call. Apple's
  framework hits these occasionally — a retry usually clears it. Worth adding a
  single retry-on-timeout path so a transient ANE blip doesn't ruin the user's
  tile-tap.

  3. Cosmetic noise (already on the NEXT_STEPS punch list, not blocking)

  - UIScene lifecycle will soon be required — pre-TestFlight cleanup item
  - _UIModernBarButton width=0 conflicts (3×) — same punch list

  Let me fix #1 right now since it's the only thing actively breaking the
  iOS-only behavior we just shipped.

