⏺ Wait — there's a context mismatch I need to resolve before touching code. Two
  things in your message don't fit Hexmind:

  - Bundle id app.alttextstudio.ios — Hexmind's bundle is app.hexmind.ios (set
  in capacitor.config.ts and the iOS target). "Alt Text Studio" is a different
  app name entirely.
  - Schemes share, test, uxtest, action, core — Hexmind doesn't have a Share
  Extension, Action Extension, or Core framework target. Those names sound like
  extension targets for an accessibility/alt-text tool, not a hex mind-mapping
  app.

  The Xcode error "Embedded binary's bundle identifier is not prefixed with the
  parent app's bundle identifier" is a real and fixable issue — every
  extension's bundle id has to start with the parent app's bundle id (e.g.
  parent app.alttextstudio.ios → share extension app.alttextstudio.ios.share).
  But I want to make sure I'm fixing it in the right repo before I touch
  anything.

