⏺ Committed 0e2d7f6. Both assets are in place and Cap-synced.

  Visual previews (the 180px and 683px thumbnails I wrote into assets/preview/):

  - AppIcon at 180×180 — yellow point-up hex with white bolt on near-black bg.
  Reads cleanly. The bolt's middle notch survives even at 60×60 (Settings-app
  size).
  - Splash at 683×683 — same mark shrunk to 24% of canvas with a soft amber glow
   halo. Stays centered through every aspect ratio iOS will throw at it.

  What you'll see in Xcode after a clean build:
  - AppIcon target slot now shows the new mark instead of the old
  orange-gradient hex
  - Launch screen / splash shows the glowing hex-on-black on cold start until
  React mounts
  - Two shared schemes in the scheme picker: App (the original Capacitor
  default) and Hexmind (the one you renamed earlier today)

  Tweak knobs in assets/build_icons.py if anything reads off:
  - BG, HEX_FILL, HEX_HIGHLIGHT, BOLT_FILL, GLOW_RGB — colors
  - hex_fraction=0.62 for icon (controls how big the hex is on the icon canvas)
  - hex_fraction=0.24 for splash (smaller, leaves room for the glow halo)
  - bolt_fraction=0.78 — bolt size relative to hex inradius

  Rebuild from Xcode → check the SpringBoard preview in the simulator. If the
  bolt feels too thin or the hex too big, change those numbers and re-run
  python3 assets/build_icons.py && npx cap sync ios.

  Open thread (paused): the embedded-binary bundle-prefix error from your Xcode
  session. The on-disk project.pbxproj still shows just one target with
  app.hexmind.ios, so the new extensions aren't saved yet. When you save Xcode
  and the new targets land in the .pbxproj, point me at it and I'll fix the
  prefix mismatch (each extension needs its bundle id to start with
  app.alttextstudio.ios., e.g. app.alttextstudio.ios.share).

