⏺ Committed 369324c. Rebuild from Xcode and you should see:

  - AppIcon — warm cream background, gold hex, white bolt. No more austere
  black.
  - Splash — same cream bg with a faint amber halo behind the centered hex.
  Spinner is now amber-on-cream instead of the previous white-on-dark.
  - No flicker on cold launch — all three surfaces (LaunchScreen.storyboard,
  Splash.imageset PNG, SplashScreen plugin's backgroundColor) now resolve to the
   same #FAF7F0.

  Still on the punch list from your launch trace (cosmetic, not blocking, can
  land in one separate commit):

  1. UIScene deprecation warning — current AppDelegate uses the legacy
  lifecycle. Apple says "will assert in a future release." Fix is ~30 min: add
  UIApplicationSceneManifest to Info.plist, create SceneDelegate.swift, trim
  AppDelegate to scene-aware shape. There's a stash from earlier (stash@{0}: 
  More stuff) that started this work — but it also touches
