⏺ Found the root cause. Capacitor 8 has nativeProjectDir = 'App'; hardcoded in
  @capacitor/cli/dist/config.js:228. There is no config option to override it.
  Every cap sync ios looks at ios/App/CapApp-SPM/ (and ios/App/App.xcworkspace)
  regardless of what's in capacitor.config.ts. The ios.scheme config I just
  added is only used for cap open ios / cap run ios, not for path lookup during
  sync.

  So the rename ios/App/ → ios/Hexmind/ is structurally incompatible with
  Capacitor 8 — it broke cap sync and triggered the CocoaPods fallback (which
  then fails because we never used CocoaPods).

  Three real options. None of them I want to execute without your approval,
  since each involves either a destructive move or a non-trivial workaround:

⏺ User answered Claude's questions:
  ⎿  · How do you want to resolve the Capacitor / rename incompatibility? → 
     Rename ios/Hexmind/ back to ios/App/ — keep Hexmind.xcodeproj inside 
     (Recommended)
     · Before I do anything destructive, is your unsaved Xcode state still in 
     the running Xcode process? → Xcode is closed — safe to move things

⏺ Moving the parent folder back. Let me verify the destination is clear first,
  then move.

