⏺ Capacitor 8's hardcoding goes deeper. From the error trace:
  - ios/App/CapApp-SPM/ ✓ now found (the parent rename worked)
  - ios/App/App.xcodeproj/project.pbxproj ❌ Capacitor expects App.xcodeproj
  literally — we have Hexmind.xcodeproj
  - ios/App/App/public ✓ created (but the inner source folder is actually
  Hexmind/, so the web bundle just got copied to a sibling empty folder, not the
   source folder Xcode references)

  So the project filename and the inner source folder are also hardcoded as 
  "App". Even with the parent rename undone, the cosmetic rename inside breaks
  two more Capacitor lookups.

  This means the user's intuition for "rename in Xcode for cosmetic reasons" was
   the wrong tool — the Hexmind label they wanted is actually achieved via the
  shared scheme name (which we already committed earlier today as
  Hexmind.xcscheme alongside App.xcscheme). The Xcode project file and source
  folder MUST stay named App for Capacitor 8 to function.

  Cleanest path forward: full structural revert. Hexmind.xcodeproj →
  App.xcodeproj, inner Hexmind/ → App/, plus revert the path = Hexmind; edit in
  pbxproj. The shared scheme Hexmind.xcscheme is the user-facing name in Xcode's
   scheme picker.

⏺ User answered Claude's questions:
