⏺ False positive on "How many hours do you have available?" — the bare ^how 
  many\b pattern catches user-knowledge questions that start the same way. Per
  the cynic's earlier ambiguity analysis, removing this pattern is the right
  tradeoff: false-positives (suppressing legitimate questions) are worse than
  false-negatives, and the rewritten prompt should rarely produce factual "how
  many" questions anyway.

