⏺ Looking at the screenshots, three things jump out:

  🐛 Critical bug — schema placeholder leaking into the modal. Screenshot 3
  shows the question literally rendered as "Question only if shouldAsk is true, 
  else omit" — that's my placeholder text from the JSON schema example in the
  system prompt. Apple FoundationModels copied it verbatim. The chips ("Global
  Fashion" / "Local Traditions") are real LLM output, but the question field
  grabbed the schema's placeholder string. This is the strongest argument yet
  for Part A.1 (@Generable) — Gemini's responseSchema.description doesn't
  pollute the output the same way because the schema is enforced separately from
   the prompt text.

  🎨 Tile look: every visible tile is "concept" type (lightbulb + amber). The 5
  type variety (concept/action/technical/question/risk → distinct icons + stroke
   colors) isn't expressing because all six branches the LLM picked happened to
  be concepts. Could be coincidence, could be the prompt under-weighting
  variety.

  🛠 Toolbar real estate: 9 icons in the main bar, with the import/export quartet
   (folder/download/upload/share) plus the second-row redo-with-download glyph
  all eating space. Consolidating all of those under the folder icon is a clean
  win.

