⏺ Committed 269a423. Rebuild from Xcode and the on-device path should produce
  parseable JSON again.

  What I changed:

  1. Tightened the type-distribution block from 13 lines to 4 — same rules (3+
  types, max 3 concepts, must include action + risk/question) but no longer
  drowning out the schema instruction.
  2. Replaced the prose CRITICAL paragraph with a concrete JSON example — 6 real
   branches showing every field, both shouldAskClarifyingQuestion: true and
  false cases. Uses realistic values ("Revenue Model", "Target Market", etc.)
  plus an explicit "do NOT copy these literally" line so the placeholder-leak
  doesn't return.

  Why this happened: removing the inline JSON example (139c4a0) + adding the
  verbose variety block (10f9c26) shifted the prompt's center of gravity away
  from JSON shape. Apple FM, with no @Generable enforcement, started emitting
  prose. The web/Android path didn't break because Gemini's responseSchema is
  grammar-enforced regardless of prompt shape.

  Permanent fix is still Part A.1 — Swift @Generable moves schema enforcement
  out of the prompt entirely, immune to this kind of regression. Without it,
  every prompt edit risks breaking the schema again.

  Want me to:
  1. Wait while you rebuild + test the prompt fix on device?
  2. Tackle Part A.1 now so this class of bug stops happening?

