  Just landed (91c2250)

  Fix: Toast position
  What: bottom-right (default) → top-center with 56px offset. Now clear of
    minimap, tour cards, and InspectPanel
  ────────────────────────────────────────
  Fix: Tour centering
  What: Was items-end pb-10 (bottom-anchored). Now items-center since the
    dim+blur backdrop already focuses attention
  ────────────────────────────────────────
  Fix: Skip always visible
  What: Was tutorialStep === 0 only. Now visible on every step, labeled "Skip
    rest"
  ────────────────────────────────────────
  Fix: Clarifying tiles emission fix
  What: The JSON example showed 1/6 with shouldAsk=true (~17%); Apple FM picked
    up the implicit cue and rounded to 0. Now shows 2/6 + explicit "EXPECTED
    FREQUENCY: 1-2 per generation" line in both prompts

  /thinkagain on the tour — what I changed vs. what I rejected

  Changed:
  - Centered (was bottom)
  - Always-visible Skip (was step 0 only)
  - Skip label disambiguated to "Skip rest"

  Considered + rejected:
  - Collapsing 5 steps to 1. The user has already seen tap-to-expand via the
  initial prompt→generate flow, so technically the first step is redundant. BUT
  cutting to 1 step would lose the auto-expand mention (which is a non-obvious
  behavior worth surfacing). Kept all 5; relied on always-visible Skip to let
  users opt out early.
  - One-tooltip-only design. Too aggressive given that the auto-expand and
  combine gestures genuinely aren't discoverable from the affordance alone.

  If you want a more aggressive trim ("just the tap card, kill the rest"), say
  the word — half a commit.

  Why clarifying tiles vanished + why this fix should restore them

  The variety prompt + 6-branch example with 1/6 ask was sending a signal: "asks
   are rare, default to false." Apple FM doesn't have @Generable to enforce
  field semantics, so the prompt's example IS the schema for it. The new 2/6
  example + explicit frequency hint should restore the 1-2-asks-per-gen pattern.
   Will be reliably fixed by Part A.1 (@Generable + GenerationGuide).

  Standing by for your push + next test pass.

