⏺ Council replan saved

  ~/.swarm/next-steps/2026-05-10-hexmind-council-replan.md — supersedes the
  priority order from /wrap.

  Three changes to the prior queue

  1. Cynic blind spot win — first-launch starter tile. There's no empty-state
  design. Tour fires only after first generation settles, which only happens if
  the user knows to tap. Pre-populate a "tap me" tile on first-ever launch.
  Ship-blocker, ~1 day.
  2. Architect timing win — prewarm() moves to pre-TestFlight. Currently in
  "Phase 3 polish." Without it, first tap on a cold launch is 4-8s on real
  hardware. Bundle with #1.
  3. Cynic ship-discipline win — defer UIScene to v1.0.1, defer trademark to 30 
  days post-launch, ship static PNGs not GIFs in the in-app tour. Apple's "will
  assert" warning has been live since iOS 13 (2019) without ever firing.
  Engineer comfort isn't user value. TEAS Plus needs real product-page
  specimens; TestFlight ones get refused.

  First 5 minutes when you're back

  Open Xcode → set destination "Any iOS Device (arm64)" → Cmd-B. Don't archive,
  don't run. Just build. The @Generable BranchSet work has never compiled
  against real iOS 26 SDK. If it fails, the fix is an explicit init(from 
  decoder:) on GeneratedBranch (~20 min). If it builds clean, plug in the iPhone
   and Run.

  Tightened kill criteria (rebaselined to corrected 35-40% TAM)

  ┌──────────────────────────────┬─────────────┬────────────────────┐
  │          Criterion           │     Old     │        New         │
  ├──────────────────────────────┼─────────────┼────────────────────┤
  │ WAU at D60                   │ <200        │ <350               │
  ├──────────────────────────────┼─────────────┼────────────────────┤
  │ D30 retention                │ <8%         │ <12%               │
  ├──────────────────────────────┼─────────────┼────────────────────┤
  │ Tour completion at D14       │ (untracked) │ <40%               │
  ├──────────────────────────────┼─────────────┼────────────────────┤
  │ Cold-start to first-tile p50 │ (untracked) │ >5s = ship-blocker │
  └──────────────────────────────┴─────────────┴────────────────────┘

  Where the council fought

  - UIScene migration timing: Architect wanted it pre-TestFlight to avoid a
  second Archive cycle. Cynic won: 6 years of "will assert" without asserting
  outweighs marginal Archive cost. Defer to v1.0.1.
  - Tour GIFs: Architect wanted parallel tracks. Cynic wanted to kill entirely.
  Verdict: SPLIT — static PNGs in-app, animated GIFs for App Store screenshots
  only.

  Single biggest unaddressed risk in the current state

  Cold-start on a real iPhone 15 Pro. Simulator hides FoundationModels warmup,
  thermal throttling, ANE asset hydration. Real first-tap will be 4-8s. Without
  prewarm AND a starter tile, the first-launch sequence is: empty grid → 3-5s
  confusion → random tap → 4-8s wait → user has swiped away by second 7-12.
  Two-day fix heads this off entirely. Skipping it is the most likely TestFlight
   failure mode.

  Have a good break. The council was tougher than I'd have been alone — that's
  the value of dispatching dissent.

